<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahmadnagar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1494</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahmadnagar is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a>, western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, founded in 1494 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-nizam-shah-i">Ahmad Nizam Shah I</a> as the capital of the Nizam Shahi sultanate. Its fort was defended by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chand-bibi">Chand Bibi</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a> in 1595 and fell to them in 1600. The city later passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a> and in 1803 to the British, who used its fort as a prison.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ahmadnagar.jpg" alt="Ahmadnagar" width="320" height="118" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rohit8596 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ahmednagarrailwaystation.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
